13:10:09.853 > l
13:10:09.922 | Arms of the Maldaathi. (indoors)
13:10:09.928 | A noxious, red-hued fog overwhelms the area with a thick, palpable vapour. This illustrious shop boasts walls of robust granite that stand as a testament to Strength and the Truths. Beneath, a darkwood floor is adorned with a meticulously crafted rug depicting intricate battle scenes, a masterpiece woven with threads that seem to tell tales of valour and conquest. Artfully placed around the shop, mannequins donned in gleaming armour catch the ambient light, creating a captivating display of martial prowess. Each piece, meticulously crafted, reflects the expert artisanship that defines the Maldaathi knights. Iron sconces, housing torches that flicker with an unwavering flame, cast a warm and inviting glow upon the space. One wall, adorned with a discreet inscription in Qith from the Apocrypha, whispers one of the Truths in subtle silver letters. Preserving the rich history of the Maldaathi knights, the proud guild flag hangs regally, a symbol of their importance within the city of Mhaldor and a constant reminder of the honour and steadfast courage that echoes through the ages. A runic totem is planted solidly in the ground. An obsidian eye sigil is here. Plodding about with a lumbering stride, a heavy workhorse meanders here. A ladder of long, soft leaves comprises a wispy Weaver's Fern along the ground. Lying flat on the ground is a key-shaped sigil. A sigil in the shape of a small, rectangular monolith is on the ground. A bejewelled suit of ornate cloth armour has been abandoned here. There are 5 Blackrock clerics here. A mortal heart, still dripping blood is here. Stretching its wings in an impressive display is an ebony pegasus, its dark coat absorbing the surrounding light. There are 5 corpses of an elite mhun keeper here. There are 2 corpses of a cunning black wolf here. There are 4 corpses of a majestic lion here. There are 2 corpses of a fairy Knight of Sidhe here. There are 3 corpses of a moon bear here. Khaqith Titonus Lichlord, the Confessor of Mhaldor is here. His face is partially concealed beneath the raised hood of a daemon-skin cloak of the Black Hand. He wields an ancient scimitar in his left hand and a blackened Maldaathi war-scimitar in his right.  You see a sign indicating there are WARES for sale here.
13:10:09.930 | You see exits leading west (closed door) and down (closed door).
